<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">King of the Universe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King of the Universe, or King of the World, was a prestigious Mesopotamian royal title signifying universal rule. First used by Akkadian kings, it was later adopted by Assyrian rulers to express claims to supremacy over all lands. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> it formed part of the ideology that justified expansion and conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-of-the-universe.jpg" alt="King of the Universe" width="297" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ALFGRN · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sargon_of_Akkad_on_his_victory_stele.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
